      "summary": "The constructor’s explicit no-op limits path can disable the investigation budgets. I found no other concrete security vulnerability in the changed code.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/BoundedInvestigator.cs",
          "line": 74,
          "message": "An explicit NoInvestigationLimits argument bypasses the required per-investigation budgets.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The constructor accepts any IInvestigationLimits implementation. If a caller passes the public NoInvestigationLimits.Instance, the fallback that creates real InvestigationLimits is skipped; its checks are no-ops.",
            "failureScenario": "If the application constructs an investigator with NoInvestigationLimits.Instance and a user submits a resource-intensive investigation, the tool, model-call, time, and token budgets are unenforced. This is an unbounded consumption risk (OWASP LLM10:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
